Description: Blur the background behind surfaces that ask for it
 Implements ext-background-effect-v1 (wayland-protocols staging): a client
 sets a blur region on a wl_surface, and the GL renderer blurs whatever is
 drawn behind that region before drawing the surface. The grab is a
 glBlitFramebuffer (glCopyTexSubImage2D on GLES2) of the region's bounding
 box, blurred with dual-Kawase down/up passes at reduced resolution, and
 drawn back weighted by the surface's own alpha, so rounded corners and
 soft shadows inside the region aren't blurred. MIR_BLUR_PASSES (1-6,
 default 3) and MIR_BLUR_OFFSET (default 2.0) tune the strength.
 .
 The region applies when set rather than on the next commit; clients set
 it and commit together, so the difference doesn't show. The shell has to
 enable "ext_background_effect_manager_v1" like any other extension.
 .
 The frontend and the renderer share the regions through
 mir::graphics::background_blur, keyed by the surface's buffer stream (the
 renderable id), exported from libmirplatform in its own version node.
 Renderer gains a private class and a private non-virtual method only.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: no
